WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.750
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:12.990
The reading from the Sinaxadion for June 9, on which we commemorate our Holy Father,

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.710
Cyril, patriarch of Alexandria.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:22.950
On the 9th of the month we celebrate the memory of our Holy Father, the God-bearer, Cyril,

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.310
archbishop of Alexandria.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:32.890
The St. Athanasius, who was the adamant defender of the Homousios, consubstantial.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:39.070
The Church of Alexandria was, for the whole world, the lighthouse of Orthodoxy, thanks to

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:46.510
St. Cyril, the champion of the Thilthocles, the mother of God, the touchstone of the dogma

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.870
of the incarnation.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:56.290
Born in about 360, he was early placed under the protection of his uncle, Philphilus, archbishop

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:02.710
of Alexandria, who gave him a complete formation in rhetoric and philosophy, and especially

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:10.630
in the Holy Scriptures, which he knew almost by heart, and was able to put to good use.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.130
Placing his great learning at the service of the Church, the young Cyril was included

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:19.670
among the clergy and called to succeed the Philphilus.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:25.410
He accompanied him to Constantinople and was present at the Iniquities Pirate Council of

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:33.090
the Oak in 403, which unjustly condemned St. John Chrysostom.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:38.890
He later refused for a long time to write St. John's name on the diptych's, more from

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:45.210
devotion to his uncle's memory than from doctrinal opposition to the Holy Hierarch, and it was

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:53.530
only on the urging of St. Isador of Palusium, and it is said after a vision of the mother

00:01:53.530 --> 00:02:00.450
of God with St. John Chrysostom beside her that he consented to put it in again, and

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:07.850
even became a fervent supporter of his veneration in 417.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:15.050
On Philphilus's death in 412, he was immediately consecrated archbishop of Alexandria, despite

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:20.850
violent opposition from the supporters of Archdecan Timothy, of an energetic character

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.850
and gifted with ardent zeal for the defense of the truth.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:30.650
St. Cyril undertook to strengthen the unity of the Church, which was at the time in full

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:36.890
flower, but was still threatened by various divisive elements.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.290
Preaching to his people the love of the true faith which had been preserved by the Holy

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:47.170
Fathers through so many battles against the heretics, he took authoritative measures

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:53.370
against the novation schismatics, who were drawing many of the orthodox to their side

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.370
because of their austerity and moral rigor.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:03.170
He had their churches closed and forbade their bishop to fulfill his functions.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:08.650
To combat the remains of paganism and the superstitions which still gripped the people,

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:17.570
he had the relics of St. Cyrus and John translated from Alexandria to Manuthus near Canope.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:23.090
Famous for its diabolically-inspired oracles and himself took the head of the procession

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.890
which lasted a whole week.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:32.010
Although Alexandria was a Christian city, it still had an important Jewish colony, which

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.930
often disturbed the peace with riots and attacks on the Christians.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.410
Following one of these incidents, the bishop summoned the heads of the Jewish community

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.370
and reprimanded them with threats.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:50.530
They in revenge, pretending there was a fire in the Church of St. Alexander, brought the Christians

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.610
together at night and slew a great many of them.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:59.890
In the face of the inertia of prefect arrestes, who, fearing the growing power of the bishop

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:06.610
in civil matters was predisposed to the Jews, St. Cyril had them all expelled from the city

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:10.410
and turned the synagogues into churches.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:15.970
It was thus that the Jewish colony in Alexandria, which had been well known since the time of Alexander

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:19.250
the Great, came to an end.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.970
But these events poisoned the archbishop's relations with the prefect.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:30.770
Some monks from Nigeria devoted to St. Cyril placed themselves one day in the magistrate's

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.050
path and called him a pagan.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:40.370
And one of them, Ammonius, grabbed a stone and threw it at his head.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:47.370
He was at once arrested and tortured with such violence that he died.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:53.810
Further disorder also followed the ignoble killing of Hepatia, a virtuous woman of great authority

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:58.650
in the realm of philosophy, who was venerated throughout the world.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:03.790
She was murdered by an unruly group of Christian fanatics, who, suspecting that she was

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:09.350
acting as a go-between for the bishop and prefect arrestes, were intent on impending

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.030
their reconciliation.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:17.790
In the midst of these troubles which spilled a great deal of blood, St. Cyril strove to have

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:23.550
justice respected and he finally achieved the recognition of the church's authority in

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.150
every aspect of city life.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:31.790
Having inherited the famous school of Alexandria and having probably been a pupil of Dittimus

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:37.190
the blind, the holy bishop devoted a great deal of his time to the writing of exegetical

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:43.510
works with allegorical and moral commentaries on details of the Old Testament, in which

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:50.470
he discerned the mystery of Christ manifested in Enigma's.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:56.230
It is this vision of the one Christ as the fulfillment of the law and the prophets that

00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:02.550
was to direct the whole of his life, and divine providence was soon to require of him that

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:10.190
he applied both on the theological level and on that of ecclesiastical activity.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:17.950
In 428 Constantinople applied to Antioch to have the priest Nestorius elevated to the patriarchal

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:24.790
C. He was known for his eloquence and for the austere life he purported to lead.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:30.550
This election was greeted with great joy, not just by the people of the capital, who hoped

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:38.470
to receive in him a new Christom, but also by the worldwide episcopate, including St. Cyril.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:46.030
However, as soon as he was consecrated, Nestorius cast off his mask of piety and revealed

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:52.990
an intemperate zeal in warring with the heretics, declaring himself ready to wreck all the towns

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:56.070
in order to drive them out.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:01.750
He soon made himself heartily disliked by his violence and pride, and began to make

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:08.190
imprudent declarations concerning the incarnation, pushing the limit of the theological tradition

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:13.990
of the School of Antioch, which stressed the distinction in the Lord's actions between

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:21.470
those that revealed his divine nature and others that belonged to his human nature, Nestorius

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:29.190
undertook to give an abstract and rationalist explanation of the incarnation, without, however,

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:37.190
making use of adequate concepts to explain the way the natures were united.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:45.030
Introducing a duality of agents between the Word of God and Christ the mere man, he asserted

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:50.870
that the characteristics of divine and human nature would have to be attributed to one or the

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.350
other.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:08:00.390
He was led as a consequence to consider that the Word had only taken on humanity as a tent,

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:08.190
an instrument, and that the Virgin Mary was not the mother of God, Phil Tocos, a title that

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:16.630
the Church's tradition had long given her, but only mother of Christ, Christ Tocos, stating

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:23.390
that one could not say that God was born of the Virgin, but is only united with him who

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.110
was born and died.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:35.790
He merely saw in Christ an exemplary man, a God-bearer, divinized in a special way by his virtues,

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:42.350
in whom God dwelt in a way similar to that in which he inspired the prophets and the saints,

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:50.630
and who was in no way the Theantropos, the God-man, who is for men the source of salvation,

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:55.110
of life, grace, and sanctification.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:09:00.750
Without ever himself speaking of two persons in Christ, he never seized attacking the concept

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:07.830
of the Phil Tocos, and one of his disciples, Bishop Dorothils, even stated one day in a sermon

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:17.990
in the presence of Nestorius, if a man says that Mary is the Phil Tocos, led him be anathema.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:23.150
This would have meant the anathematization of all the God-bearing fathers who had used

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:30.310
the term and the bishops the world over who confessed the divine motherhood.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:37.070
Conformed of this nascent heresy, Cyril solemnly set forth in his Paschal homily the following

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:45.190
year, in 429, that the Virgin had truly given birth to the Son of God, made man, and that she

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:49.950
therefore must rightly be called the Theantocos.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:55.870
He wrote Nestorius a letter of brotherly remonstrance, asking him to accept the title on which

00:09:55.870 --> 00:10:00.150
the whole doctrine of our salvation in Christ rested.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:06.270
Even in the face of Nestorius' haughty and disdainful refusal, who, turning the accusations

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:11.270
against the archbishop of Alexandria, spread columnlies about him and attempted to have him

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:18.190
formally denounced, Cyril resolved to take up arms in defense of the truth, and declared

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:25.950
himself ready to suffer anything, even to death, rather than abandon the faith.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:33.590
He addressed the treaties on the true faith to Emperor Theodosius I, his wife and sisters,

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:39.390
and sent a dossier on Nestorius' errors to Pope Celestine.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:45.910
The Pope convoked a council in Rome, which condemned the errors and charged the archbishop of Alexandria

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:52.190
with carrying out the sentence pronounced against the heretic, if he refused to retract with

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.750
in ten days, in 430.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:02.230
In the meantime, Saint Cyril had summoned a synod of bishops of Egypt, which wrote an exposé

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:08.790
of Christological doctrine, followed by the twelve anathemas of Nestorius' propositions

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:13.470
that Cyril had addressed to the heretic in his third letter.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:19.390
In these polemical writings against Nestorius, faithful to the holy writ on the word made flesh

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:25.910
and to the fathers of the council of Nicaea who had confessed that the same son of God remaining

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:31.590
in the bosom of the Father became man, died and rose again.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:36.830
Saint Cyril underlined the unity of the mystery of Christ.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:43.430
He strove to show that from the first moment of his conception, the Lord definitively united

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:51.350
human and divine nature, and he contemplates in this mysterious union, Hennoses, with no

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:59.870
conjunction, Sinaphia, as Nestorius asserted, the exchange of natural properties and unity

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:08.190
of action of the Savior, who has opened to men the possibility of true participation with God,

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:16.110
of deification, of which the Mother of God is the prototype and model.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:23.190
The Lord having thus inaugurated a new mode of existence, divine and human together in his

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:30.950
body, the Church, it is from his flesh truly become the flesh of the Word that we are given

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.470
life.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:41.270
The one Christ of Saint Cyril is then he of the Eucharist and of spiritual experience, which

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:49.870
at the cost of long and difficult controversies the Church was to define in the succeeding generations.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:55.750
During this time, Nestorius, relying on imperial authority and his friends at court, attempted

00:12:55.750 --> 00:13:02.230
to impose his ideas in the capital by means of threats, corruption, excommunication

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:05.870
and the persecution of any who dared to resist him.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:11.470
The situation became such that the Orthodox clergy begged Thildosios to convoke an ecumenical

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:18.790
council to put an end to this universal scandal of the Bishop of Constantinople.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:26.670
But by a skillful twist, it was the heretic who persuaded the sovereign to summon the council,

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:34.630
to take place in Ephesus at Pentecost the following year in 431, in order to charge Saint Cyril

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:39.110
with heresy for his anathemas.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:44.670
Cyril and Nestorius, having arrived in Ephesus at the heads of imposing entorages, they

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:50.950
awaited the coming of Archbishop John of Antioch and the Eastern bishops, whom Nestorius

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.670
had won over to his cause.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:59.350
This was not because of the rejection of the term Thildocos, but by his sending them Cyril's

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:05.950
anathemas, which they could only read out of context, as though they were a restoration

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.270
of the Apollonarius' heresy.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:14.550
Finally, as they were late, it was decided to open the first session without the orientals

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:19.150
on the 22nd of June in 431.

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:25.670
Saint Cyril presided, standing in for the Pope of Rome, whose legates were also late.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:30.990
After having had the Nicene Creed read, and then Cyril's letter to Nestorius, and the

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:38.830
letters reply, the fathers who numbered about 200 proclaimed the legitimacy of the term Thildocos,

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:44.790
and opposed Nestorius, who had three times refused to appear.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:49.990
On leaving the church, they were welcomed with an ovation by a crowd devoted to the veneration

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:56.870
of the Mother of God, with women burning incense along their path.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:15:03.070
Directly on the arrival in Ephesus of John of Antioch and his party, five days later, he

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:10.070
offended that they had not been waited for, convoked a council of 43 bishops, and accusing

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:17.350
Cyril of having revived the heresy of Apollonarius pronounced his deposition with no other formality

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:22.150
than the acquiescence of Memnon of Ephesus.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:28.070
The ecumenical council thus found itself transformed into a violent and passionate battle between

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:32.710
two parties that were trying to get the Emperor's protection.

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:41.030
A luth and ill informed Thodosius, after feudal attempts at reconciliation, had Cyril and Memnon

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:48.550
arrested while declaring Nestorius a heretic, and ordered that the assembly be disbanded.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:54.910
The only result of the council was that it set out the firm grounds for the term Thildocos,

00:15:54.910 --> 00:16:00.950
and proceeded to the deposition of Nestorius, who was sent to his monastery in Antioch

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:09.110
and then exiled to Libya in 435, where he died a miserable death.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:14.670
They found themselves nonetheless, faced with a new and cruel division, at the moment at

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:20.550
which the Empire, threatened by the barbarians, was a need of the greatest cohesion.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:27.350
There could be seen only quarrels, mutual anathemas, and disorder, under the pretext of devotion

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:34.430
to the truth, that exposed the holiness of the Church to the mockery of its enemies.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:40.150
During the laborious negotiations that followed, St. Cyril, who had returned to Alexandria where

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:47.390
the people gave him a triumphant welcome, showed not only his orthodoxy, but also his humility

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:52.750
and the abundance of his virtue, refusing to demand justice for the ill treatment he had

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:58.470
received in Ephesus during his imprisonment, he gave the orientals an explanation of the

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:04.750
anathemas that had offended them so deeply, and he stated that they were only against Nestorius'

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:11.110
heretical dogmas, also declaring that he was ready to correct them, on condition that John

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:15.510
and his party consented to Nestorius' condemnation.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:21.270
They finally reached an agreement, and the orientals sent Cyril a confession of faith

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:24.790
that he welcomed with a jubilant letter.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:30.230
In a spirit of peace, but without abandoning his fundamental thesis, he made judicious

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:37.190
concessions to Antioch's traditional terminology, and accepted the distinction that was made there

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:47.230
of the two natures united without confusion or co-mingling in the unique person of Jesus Christ.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:54.310
This act of union created in April 433, although it was not a conciliar decision, is nevertheless

00:17:54.310 --> 00:18:02.710
considered as the profession of faith of the third ecumenical counsel and the rule of orthodoxy.

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:10.430
It refuted in advance the heretical proposals of Yudikes and the monophysites, who claimed

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:16.810
that some of the writings of Saint Cyril supported their belief that the human nature of Christ

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:24.990
is, as though absorbed by the divinity and the counsel of Calcedon in 451, was only held

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:30.790
to reassert and precise its essential terms.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:36.870
A fragile peace being established, Saint Cyril spent the last years of his episcopate in confirming

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:43.910
the unity of the Church and in moderating the excesses of his two zealous partisans, who accused

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:49.390
him of betraying their cause by the union with the orientals.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:56.110
In Eward to strive by his experience of ecclesiastical affairs and human passions, he showed himself

00:18:56.110 --> 00:19:02.730
in those circumstances a model of moderation and pastoral clemency.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:08.730
In this way he refuted the writings of Theodore of Mopswesta, the great theologian of the School

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:17.390
of Antioch, who died in the peace of the Church in 428, but refused to demand his condemnation,

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:22.790
in order not to upset the sensibilities of the orientals again, and so put the unity

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:26.430
of the Church in danger.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:31.750
Having finished the work that God had confided to him for the edification of his Church, Saint

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:40.470
Cyril fell asleep in peace on the 27th of June in 444, to join the choir of the Holy Fathers

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:47.830
and to take his seat together with Saint John Chrysostom alongside the Mother of God.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:55.690
He was at once venerated as a saint and praised as the Enlightener of the world, the Invincible

00:19:55.690 --> 00:20:01.510
Defender of Orthodoxy and the Seal of the Fathers.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:07.390
Through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.390
and save us.
